  "adaptation": "Affine quantized mul with channel-vector broadcasting over a [2,4] tensor.\n\nAll values and zero-points are signed INT8. RNE(x/2^e) rounds to the nearest integer, ties to the even integer, before adding the output zero-point; Clip8 saturates to [-128,127]. There is no intermediate saturation or double rounding. A has shape [2,4], B shape [4]. Dequantized A=(a-za)/2^shift_a and B=(b-zb)/2^shift_b. Output scale is one and output shape is [2,4]; its value is Clip8(RNE(A * B)+zy). The three zero points are independently supplied; shifts range 0..7. B[c] is reused by both rows. This is DequantizeLinear → Mul → QuantizeLinear with exact dyadic scales.",
  "difficulty": "medium"
}
